  "summary": "California Highway Patrol, at Gov. Newsom's direction, is installing 480 Flock Safety ALPR cameras on Oakland streets and East Bay freeways, with a 28-day retention limit and data sharing restricted to California law enforcement. Privacy advocates from EFF and Oakland's Privacy Advisory Commission criticized the deployment as mass surveillance.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The California Highway Patrol provided additional details to SFGATE about the 480 surveillance cameras set to be installed on Oakland streets and six East Bay freeways",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "The company allows data retention up to 60 days, but CHP's contract will only allow it to collect, store and share data from the cameras for up to 28 days.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "I just hope people understand \u2014 going from 300 cameras to now almost 500 \u2014 a really significant amount of location data is now going to be in the hands of the state",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    }
  ],
